From 81acf09b1a31b87091a0997ab965c7f6b8623ac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:03:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] disk_state: prepare finalized overlay keys and leaves in
 parallel

Recover the missing parallel CommitFinalizedOverlay preparation selected by original native v2/029 from 72d462e54c2f287941e3bff0061bcc1e1ee5fd57.

Original subject: perf(v2): one-wave batch MemPoolAccept, DiskState SMT fastpath, ExportSmtNode reuse, and windowed reverse peel

Run only immutable OutpointKey and Leaf preparation on independent worker slots. Apply every erase and insert in the existing order through AuthCheckCoin and the existing authenticated tree mutation and Set paths. Preserve per-item preparation errors until their serial operation is reached. Keep current ParseNode, unchanged-sibling authentication, atomic writes, undo, recovery, metadata binding and C17a coin encoding.

The historical ParseNodeFast and coin-row/sibling authentication bypasses are deliberately excluded. The true provenance owner is the disk-state preparation purpose of original native v2/029, not the unrelated earlier disk-cache or packed-record owners.

Coordinator adaptation: exact input applied on validated510; no production callers of CommitFinalizedOverlay exist. Authentication, serial mutation order and codec implementations remain authoritative. This is not a node-throughput claim. Original author provenance retained.

